# Copy to .env for local development, or set these in the Cloudflare Pages
# project's environment variables for production. Both are optional: with
# neither set the site builds and ships exactly as it does today, with no
# tracking of any kind.
#
# Both are PUBLIC_ prefixed because Astro exposes them to the browser. Neither
# is a secret — a Pixel ID is visible to anyone viewing the page source by
# design. Do not put anything genuinely secret behind a PUBLIC_ name.
#
# NOTE: none of this touches the iOS app. The app has no analytics SDK, no
# account, and no server. These variables affect the marketing site only.

# Meta (Facebook/Instagram) Pixel ID, from Meta Events Manager.
# Leave empty until Business Manager exists. While empty:
#   - no Meta script is added to the page
#   - no <noscript> tracking image is rendered
#   - no Meta network request is made
# Setting it does NOT start tracking on its own — the pixel still loads only
# after a visitor actively accepts in the consent banner.
PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=

# Apple App Analytics provider token, from App Store Connect →
# App Analytics → Campaigns. Optional.
# When set, App Store links carry `pt=<token>`; when empty the parameter is
# omitted entirely and `ct` alone still gives campaign-level attribution.
# This is a URL parameter Apple reads server-side — it is not client-side
# tracking and is not consent-gated.
PUBLIC_APPLE_PT=
